EXECUTIVE SUMMARY: THE TERMINAL ARCHITECTURAL SINGULARITY\uc0\u8232 The Axion Phantom-Stratum (APS) v.1.0.0-OMEGA represents the terminal evolution of high-performance computing on the x86-64 architecture. While previous iterations successfully isolated the OS-scheduler and partitioned the L3 cache, they remained vulnerable to systemic fragility, micro-architectural "butterfly effects," and electrical cross-talk. APS v.1.0.0-OMEGA resolves these final frontiers by introducing Mathematical Formal Verification (MFV) to the isolation logic and Power-Plane Decoupling (PPD) to the physical silicon. By unifying the compiler (Axion-LLVM), the memory controller, and the power delivery system into a single, verified execution stratum, APS v.1.0.0-OMEGA achieves absolute, 10/10-class determinism. It is no longer a "tuned" system; it is a mathematically proven, autonomous sanctuary where hardware and software are synthesized into a single, predictable entity, immune to the noise of Ring -2 firmware and PCIe fabric congestion.\
