PHASE I: FORMALLY VERIFIED SILICON ISOLATION (MFV-HAL)\uc0\u8232 To eliminate the fragility of manual memory-tuning and the "Compilation Wall," APS v.1.0.0-OMEGA implements a formally verified micro-kernel substrate.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Mathematical Proof of Isolation\
The HAL 2.0 logic for Page Coloring and vDCA (Virtual Direct Cache Access) is verified against the hardware's TLB (Translation Lookaside Buffer) and L3-set-associativity tables using Coq and Isabelle/HOL formal proofs.\
Logic: This ensures that no memory allocation on the Core-Ghetto can ever map to a cache set reserved for the Phantom-process, regardless of kernel-level entropy or fragmentation.\
B. Axion-LLVM Compiler Synthesis\
APS v.1.0.0-OMEGA utilizes a customized LLVM-based compiler chain. It injects "Determinism Metadata" into the binary, ensuring that "Warm-up" sequences and Page Coloring offsets are preserved through the entire optimization pipeline.\
Result: This prevents the compiler from optimizing away critical cache-priming instructions, ensuring that the machine code matches the mathematical model of the stratum.\
