PHASE II: POWER-PLANE DECOUPLING (PPD) AND ELECTRICAL SILENCE\uc0\u8232 To eliminate the subtle "butterfly effect" of electrical noise from the Core-Ghetto (Cores 0-1) affecting the Phantom-cores (Cores 2-N), APS v.1.0.0-OMEGA enforces independent voltage domain control.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Vcore Domain Isolation\
Utilizing Intel FIVR (Fully Integrated Voltage Regulators) or AMD SVI3 interfaces, APD v.1.0.0-OMEGA drops Ghetto-core voltages (V_ghetto) to the absolute "Deep-Idle" floor (V_min).\
Equation 1: Electrical Noise Reduction (N_elec)\
N_elec = 1 - (V_ghetto_delta / V_phantom_stable)\
By maintaining a stable, high-voltage plane for the Phantom-cores while starving the Ghetto-cores of transient current, APS eliminates Vdroop-induced jitter and electrical cross-talk.\
B. Thermal Gradient Balancing (TGC 2.0)\
The Fail-Safe Watchdog (FSW 2.0) monitors the thermal delta between the Ghetto and Phantom clusters. If a "Thermal Bloom" is detected from the Ghetto, the FSW executes an "Interrupt-Vent," briefly pausing Ghetto-execution to ensure the Phantom-cores remain at a constant, jitter-free temperature of 51.5C.\
