PHASE III: RING -2 SMI-SHIELDING (TERMINAL ENFORCEMENT)\uc0\u8232 System Management Interrupts (SMIs) represent the final "Invisible Wall" of firmware interference. APS v.1.0.0-OMEGA implements a hardware-enforced shield.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. SMM-Lock and Timeout Enforcement\
Leveraging Intel "SMI-Priority" and AMD "SMM-Lock" bits in the BIOS/UEFI substrate, APD v.1.0.0-OMEGA creates a hardware-enforced window where Ring -2 interrupts are physically blocked or deferred for up to 500 microseconds.\
Logic: If a critical compute pulse is active, the firmware is prohibited from entering SMM-mode until the pulse is completed.\
Equation 2: Firmware Jitter Bound (J_fw)\
J_fw = Integral(SMI_events) dt -> 0 during Pulse_window.\
