\cf0 A. I/O Fabric Priority (The Omega-Link)\
Utilizing PCIe ATS (Address Translation Services) and PASID (Process Address Space ID), APS ensures that incoming NIC-data is routed with 100% priority directly to the Phantom-process L3-ways.\
Result: This eliminates the "Memory Bus Contention" jitter caused by background NVMe or GPU traffic.\
B. Data Direct I/O (DDIO) Optimization\
APS forces DDIO to inject incoming packets directly into the L3-Cache (Ways 0-7), bypassing the 60ns DRAM latency wall. The cache ways are cloistered specifically for the target PID, ensuring "Zero-Copy" execution from the wire to the ALU.\
